hout <i>tarbit</i>, and <i>tarbit</i> without <i>neshekh</i>?</b> The term <i>neshekh</i>, from a root meaning bite, connotes loss to the borrower, while the term <i>tarbit</i>, literally increase, connotes profit for the lender. The Gemara asks: <b>What are the circumstances</b> where there could be <b><i>neshekh</i> without <i>tarbit</i>?</b>"]],"w":{"0":"And can you understand","1":"that there is","2":"neshekh","3":"without","4":"tarbit","5":"and tarbit","6":"without","7":"neshekh","8":"neshekh","9":"without","10":"tarbit","11":"What are the circumstances"},"g":[[0,1,"וכי יכול אתה לסבור, להבין כך","a"],[1,2,"שיש","a"],[10,13,"כיצד יכול להיות","a"]]},{"k":"fffb4564641b","n":36,"p":[[0,1,"If"],[1,2,"one lends to"],[2,4,"one hundred … with","<b>one hundred</b> <i>perutot</i> <b>with</b>"],[3,6,"one hundred and twenty, … initially one hundred","<b>one hundred and twenty,</b> and <b>initially one hundred</b>"],[6,7,"are"],[7,9,"one-sixth [<i>bedanka</i>]"],[9,11,"and ultimately,"],[11,13,"one hundred and twenty"],[13,14,"are … one-sixth","<b>are</b> worth <b>one-sixth</b>"],[14,20,"there is <i>neshekh</i>, as … reduces … since","<b>there is <i>neshekh</i>, as</b> the lender <b>reduces</b> the borrower’s assets <b>since</b>"],[20,21,"takes"],[21,22,"from"],[22,25,"that he did not give"],[25,30,"and there is no <i>tarbit</i>, as there is no profit"],[30,32,"since he lent him one-sixth"],[32,36,"and he received from him one-sixth"]],"w":{"0":"If","1":"one lends to","2":"one hundred","3":"with … one hundred … one hundred","4":"and twenty","5":"initially","6":"are","7":"one","8":"sixth","9":"and ultimately","11":"one hundred","12":"and twenty","13":"are … one sixth","14":"neshekh","15":"there is","16":"as","17":"reduces … since","20":"takes","21":"from","22":"that he","23":"did not","24":"give","25":"and … tarbit","26":"there is no … there is","27":"as … no","29":"profit","30":"since he … one sixth","31":"lent him","32":"and … received from him one sixth","33":"he"},"g":[[