6bba8b","n":18,"p":[[0,4,"If you go according to the initial"],[5,10,"there is neither <i>neshekh</i> nor is there <i>tarbit</i>,"],[10,15,"If you go according to the ultimate"],[15,18,"there is <i>neshekh</i> and there is <i>tarbit</i>,"]],"w":{"0":"If","2":"to the","3":"you go according … initial","5":"neither neshekh","6":"there is","7":"nor","8":"is … tarbit","9":"there","10":"If","13":"you go according … ultimate","14":"to the","15":"neshekh","16":"there is … and there is","17":"tarbit"},"g":[[0,4,"אם אחר ההתחלה אתה הולך","a"],[6,7,"יש","a"],[9,10,"יש","a"],[10,12,"אם אחר","a"],[12,14,"אתה הולך","a"]]},{"k":"95f51ffeaee5","n":22,"p":[[0,12,"Rather, Rava said: You do not find <i>neshekh</i> without <i>tarbit</i> nor <i>tarbit</i> without <i>neshekh</i>, and the verse distinguished"],[14,22,"them only so that … violating two prohibitions.","<b>them only so that</b> lending with interest always involves <b>violating two prohibitions.</b>"]],"w":{"0":"Rather","2":"Rava said","4":"You do","5":"find","6":"not","7":"neshekh … neshekh","8":"without … without … and the","9":"tarbit … tarbit … verse","10":"nor … distinguished","15":"them","17":"only","18":"so that … violating","20":"two","21":"prohibitions"},"g":[[3,4,"אין","m"]]},{"k":"0f7a79b405be","n":33,"p":[[0,3,"The Sages taught"],[3,13,"“You shall not give him your money with <i>neshekh</i> and with <i>marbit</i> you shall not give him your food”"],[13,14,"I have"],[14,15,"only"],[15,16,"<i>neshekh</i> for"],[16,18,"money and … <i>ribit</i> for … food.","<b>money and</b> a prohibition of <b><i>ribit</i> for</b> a loan of <b>food.</b>"],[18,19,"From where"],[19,25,"<i>neshekh</i> with regard to … food … verse states: … <i>neshekh</i> of food, … From where … <i>ribit</i> with regard to","<b><i>neshekh</i> with regard to</b> a loan of <b>food</b> as well? The <i>baraita</i> answers: A different <b>verse states:</b> “You shall not lend with interest [<i>tashikh</i>] to your brother: <i>Neshekh</i> of money, <b><i>neshekh</i> of food,</b> <i>neshekh</i> of anything that is lent with interest [<i>asher yishakh</i>]” (Deuteronomy 23:20). The <i>baraita</i> continues: <b>From where</b> is it derived that there is <b><i>ribit</i> with regard to</b>"],[27,33,"money? The verse states: “<i>Neshekh</i> of money.”"]],"w":{"0":"The Sages taught","3":"You shall","4":"not","5":"give","6":"him","7":"money with neshekh … with","8":"your … and … marbit you shall","9":"not","10":"give","11":"him your food","13":"I have","14":"only","15":"neshekh for","16":"money","17":"and … ribit for … food","18":"From where","19":"neshekh … neshekh","20":"with regard to … food … of food … ribit with regard","21":"From where … to","22":"verse","23":"states","27":"money","28":"The","29":"verse","30":"states","31":"Neshekh","32":"of money"},"g":[[0,2,"שנו חכמים","a"]]}]}
